# XSH strcasecmp() and strcasecmp_l()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests run in the POSIX locale (setlocale(LC_ALL, "C")); only the
# portable character set is examined. The _l forms are tested with a locale
# object from newlocale() for "C"; a failure to make one is UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XSH.strcasecmp.001
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
says       strcasecmp() returns 0 for strings that differ only in case, in the
           POSIX locale: "abc" and "ABC", "AbC" and "aBc", "a1_" and "A1_", two
           empty strings, each of the 26 letters in the two cases, and the
           whole alphabet, digits and punctuation in lowercase against the same
           in uppercase.
test       t/001-equal.c

assertion  XSH.strcasecmp.002
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
says       In the POSIX locale strcasecmp() orders strings as a byte comparison
           after conversion to lowercase would: the sign for every pair of
           single letters in either case follows the order of the lowercase
           letters, a punctuation character against a letter of either case
           follows the codes of the punctuation character and of the lowercase
           letter (so "[" against "A" is judged as against "a"), digits against
           letters and against digits follow their codes, and the first
           difference decides regardless of what follows.
note       The expected sign comes from comparing the portable-character
           literals as unsigned chars.
test       t/002-order.c

assertion  XSH.strcasecmp.003
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
says       strcasecmp() treats the end of a string as lower than any character:
           "ab" is before "ABC" and "ABC" after "ab", "" before "a" and "A"
           after "", "abc" before "ABCD"; and the result for swapped arguments
           has the opposite sign, for every pair of a set of eight strings.
test       t/003-length.c

assertion  XSH.strcasecmp.004
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      2008
says       strcasecmp_l() with a locale object for the POSIX locale gives the
           same results as strcasecmp(): 0 for case variants, the order of the
           lowercased bytes (letters, punctuation, digits) and the
           end-of-string rules.
note       The locale object comes from newlocale(); UNRESOLVED if it cannot be
           made.
test       t/004-locale-object.c

assertion  XSH.strcasecmp.005
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/strcasecmp.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap07.html#7.3.1.1
class      required
since      2024
says       In the POSIX locale errno is left unchanged by strcasecmp() and
           strcasecmp_l() on valid input, for equal, lower and greater results.
note       Issue 8 sentence (defect 448); errno is preset to a value and
           compared afterwards.
test       t/005-errno.c
